                 L A T E N T  -  8k intro

  title ....... Turbo Boost
  type ........ 8k intro, WebGL2, single HTML file (7,828 bytes)
  code ........ Claude Opus 5.5
  music ....... Claude Opus 5.5 - 80s TV action theme, 128 BPM, C minor
  harness ..... Claude Code
  runs on ..... Edge / Chrome on Windows, double-click intro.html

  A night drive for the talking car of 1982. A black wedge with
  a red scanner in its nose, a wet desert highway, an LED
  dashboard with a voice box, a green vector screen, a tunnel
  of scanner lamps, a turbo boost over a barricade, lightning
  over the mesas on every stab, and at dawn a ramp up into a
  trailer.

  The scanner sweeps once per beat; the same formula pans its
  whoosh from ear to ear in the soundtrack. The voice box shows
  the syllables the robot voice sings.

  A homage to Knight Rider (1982-86). Nothing from the show is
  used: the car, the theme and every sound are new.

  credits: box SDF after I. Quilez, ACES fit by K. Narkowicz,
  hashes by D. Hoskins and M. O'Neill (PCG), vowel formants
  after Peterson & Barney, FDN reverb after Jot & Chaigne.
  Loader and synth method from Latent's Wavefolder.

